Third-party components
----------------------

None. Minutes has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on
25/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used to write the minutes

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

On recording and transcription
------------------------------

Both specs this app absorbs forbid the same thing: no audio capture and no transcription. There is
none here — no MediaRecorder, no speech API, no transcription service. The app structures what the
person types, which is why it works with the microphone off, in a room with no signal, and on a
machine with no battery left. Topic times come from the moments the person pressed "Mark a new topic
now"; pasted minutes carry no clock, and the app does not invent one.
